'''Nyikina''' (also '''Nyigina''', '''Njigina''') is an [[Australian Aboriginal languages|Australian Aboriginal language]] of [[Western Australia]], spoken by the [[Nyigina people]].

[[Warrwa language|Warrwa]] may have been a dialect.

==Classification==
[[R. M. W. Dixon]] (2002) regards Nyikina, [[Warrwa language|Warrwa]], [[Yawuru language|Yawuru]] and [[djugun language|Jukun]] as a single language.

Nyikina is placed in the [[Nyulnyulan languages|Nyulnyulan family]] of [[non-Pama–Nyungan languages]].
